To draw a chessboard representing a FEN notation in LaTeX, you can use the `chessboard` package. Below is the complete LaTeX code including the necessary packages and commands. You simply need to replace the `setfen` value with your specific FEN string.

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{chessboard}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}

\begin{document}

\begin{center}
    % Replace the FEN string below with your specific position
    \chessboard[
        setfen=rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR,
        maxfield=h8
    ]
\end{center}

\end{document}
```

To use this:
1.  Save the code as a `.tex` file (e.g., `chess.tex`).
2.  Replace the `setfen=...` part with your actual FEN notation.
3.  Compile the file using a LaTeX editor (like Overleaf, TeXShop, or TeXworks). Ensure your compiler supports the `chessboard` package (usually pdfLaTeX or LuaLaTeX works well).

